From ReAct Prompting to Modern Tool Calling
🔧 Tool Calling Exercise: From ReAct Prompting to Modern Tool Calling



Welcome to the LangChain Tool Calling Exercise!  This exercise demonstrates the evolution from traditional ReAct prompting to modern LLM tool calling capabilities.

This excerise is based on: https://python.langchain.com/docs/concepts/tool_calling/

📚 What You'll Learn

In this exercise, you'll modernize an AI agent by transitioning from:

Old Approach: ReAct prompting with manual text parsing

New Approach: Native LLM tool calling with vendor optimization



🎯 Exercise Overview

The Problem with ReAct Prompting

The original code uses a ReAct prompt template that:

Relies on specific text formatting:
(Question/Thought/Action/Action Input/Observation)

Requires complex output parsing with ReActSingleInputOutputParser

Depends on prompt engineering for tool selection

Is brittle and can fail with minor format changes



The Modern Solution: Tool Calling

Modern LLMs support native tool calling that:

✅ Shifts responsibility to LLM vendors (they optimize tool selection)

✅ Eliminates prompt fragility (no specific format required)

✅ Provides structured responses (JSON tool calls instead of text parsing)

✅ Improves reliability (vendor-optimized decision making)



🛠 Your Mission

Replace the ReAct prompt-based approach with modern tool calling by implementing these functions:



Functions to Implement:

implement_set_api_key(api_key: str)

implement_create_model_with_tools(tools: List[Tool]) -> ChatOpenAI

implement_check_for_tool_calls(response: AIMessage) -> bool

implement_execute_tool_call(tool_call: Dict, available_tools: List[Tool]) -> str

implement_run_agent_with_tool_calling(...) -> str



🎉 Expected Output

When working correctly, your agent should:

- Set up the API key ✅

- Create a model with tool calling capabilities ✅

- Process the question: *"What is the length of the word: DOG"* ✅

- Make a tool call to `get_text_length` with `text="DOG"` ✅

- Return the result: `3` ✅



💡 Key Learning Points

Vendor Optimization: LLM providers optimize tool calling better than manual prompts

Structured Responses: Tool calls return JSON instead of requiring text parsing 

Authentic Behavior: When making tool calls, `response.content` is empty (matches real OpenAI API)

Reliability: Less dependent on prompt engineering and text formatting

Simplicity: Cleaner code with fewer moving parts

Future-Proof: Aligns with how modern AI systems work

